Any matrix $matbold(M)$ decomposes as $matbold(M) = matbold(S) + matbold(A)$ with $matbold(S)$ symmetric and $matbold(A)$ antisymmetric. Since $vb(x)^TT matbold(A) vb(x) = 0$ for antisymmetric $matbold(A)$ and all $vb(x) in RR^n$,

$ vb(x)^TT matbold(M) vb(x) = vb(x)^TT matbold(S) vb(x), $

which is why only symmetric matrices need appear in the definition of quadratic forms.
